    "narrative": "Our offensive engine for June 30th is spearheaded by **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **Corbin Carroll** (72.80), both of whom benefit significantly from facing favorable matchups against the pitching staff. **Mickey Moniak** is our top overall play, utilizing a massive +14% platoon boost and a +8% order bump to exploit the matchup against the right-handed P\u00e9rez. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** maintains elite utility; his speed profile remains the cornerstone of our strategy, and his premium spot in the #3 hole against the right-handed Roupp makes him a must-start despite a modest park factor. **Brice Turang** (72.70) also deserves a high-leverage tag, as his +19% SP skill advantage against Lowder provides the highest non-park-adjusted efficiency boost in the lineup today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Isaac Paredes** (45.95), who sat just shy of our threshold despite a strong projection. While his dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed Ryan is valuable, his efficiency was cannibalized by a poor -19% SP skill rating, relegating him behind the more favorable offensive environments occupied by **Austin Riley** and **Max Muncy**. We are keeping a close eye on **Jose Caballero** (56.01), whose score is buoyed by a aggressive +13% platoon split; however, he faces an immense challenge in Skubal, whose elite 2.78 xERA represents the most significant risk to our daily total. \n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with **Dalton Rushing** (47.65) and **Kyle Karros** (48.80), both of whom are fringe starters hovering near the 40-point floor. **Dalton Rushing** is penalized by a -9% platoon disadvantage and an -8% order drag while hitting in the #9 spot. We are also monitoring **James Wood** (56.55); while his raw speed against the opposing pitcher is a clear positive for our stolen base pursuit, his score is severely hampered by a -16% SP skill penalty, suggesting that while he may contribute to our SB targets, his overall production may fluctuate against Early.",
